  "notes": "Guitar-first producer of the 2020s pop-punk and melodic-rap revival. The Lane line names the pop-punk mode first and gives it both its class and its band — \"the pop-punk mode is 140—170 with the backbeat on 2&4 straight, the melodic-rap mode 130—150 half-time\" — so this model is straight at 140—170 while his duo partner's entry sits lower and wider; that is the honest difference between two producers who share a room, and no other difference is invented. The kit is the entry's: \"pop-punk kit — driving 8th-note kick, snare hard on 2&4, crash on chorus downbeats — layered over programmed 808 and trap hats on the rap-facing records.\" So `offbeat8thShare` is 0.46, the highest in this batch (a driving 8th-note kick is exactly that number), the snare is the hardest transient here with no clap layer, `crash` leads the percs at `downbeat`, and the trap hats survive as a 32nd roll vocabulary. The low end follows the guitar rather than the kick, which the entry says outright: \"808 sub doubled by a distorted electric bass; the bass follows the guitar's root rhythm rather than the kick.\" So `lockTo808` stays low and the bassline is `independent_riff` at a high `followRootsProb` — following roots, but not the kick — with `bass808` as `counter_riff` doubling it. Harmony is \"minor-mode guitar keys with power-chord voicings and a i—VI—III—VII loop as the default\", so `triad` is 0.82, the highest authored in this section, because a power chord is less than a triad. His documented identity is that he \"could speak through the instrument — the guitar line, not the chord chart, is the idea\", which is why the counter is `answer_lick` at top weight and the arrangement uses \"the distortion switch as the lift\" rather than a drum change. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 155 (the midpoint of the stated 140—170 pop-punk band) are INFERRED.",
